sec.p:
For renal injury in patients with HFrEF, only SGLT2i treatment was associated with a lower risk of renal injury (40%) when compared with placebo (Figure

7A
). Meanwhile, the incidence of renal injury caused by SGLT2i was lower than that caused by RASi and ARNI (Figure

7A
). Compared with RASi, ARNI could significantly reduce renal injury risk (RR = 0.87, 95% CI 0.77–0.99) (Figure

7A
). However, for renal injury in patients with HFpEF, there were no differences in the occurrence of renal injury of the three treatments when compared with placebo or each other (Figure

7B
).
